WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.083 --> 00:00:04.129
So it looks like we got some animal activity already. 

00:00:04.129 --> 00:00:05.755
Hold on. Don't come down any further.

00:00:16.266 --> 00:00:19.310
We're here at
probably one of the most beautiful spots

00:00:19.310 --> 00:00:22.605
that you can see in Big Bend
National Park, Santa Elena Canyon.

00:00:24.315 --> 00:00:29.738
I am scouting for National Geographic
right now, looking for some native wildlife.

00:00:30.280 --> 00:00:32.323
You get a lot of swifts coming through here.

00:00:32.323 --> 00:00:33.491
There's warblers.

00:00:33.491 --> 00:00:35.785
Right now it's the peregrine falcon migration.

00:00:36.077 --> 00:00:38.413
It's a birders’ paradise.

00:00:41.291 --> 00:00:42.417
Being a photographer

00:00:42.417 --> 00:00:46.755
is all about putting yourself in position
to capture the best images.

00:00:48.339 --> 00:00:50.717
Sometimes the being there is the hard part

00:00:50.717 --> 00:00:53.386
because the access can be extremely challenging.

00:00:53.386 --> 00:00:55.597
But I have everything I need.

00:00:55.597 --> 00:00:59.559
I want to see if I can reach
some of these harder to get to areas.

00:01:00.310 --> 00:01:03.396
We're on our way right now
to meet Ranger Tom.

00:01:03.396 --> 00:01:06.066
Park Rangers not only understand
the layout of the place,

00:01:06.066 --> 00:01:09.069
but they know exactly
the behavior of the animal that you're

00:01:09.069 --> 00:01:12.072
trying to find, and exactly where to find it.

00:01:13.323 --> 00:01:14.115
All right.

00:01:14.115 --> 00:01:14.991
How you doing, Tom?

00:01:14.991 --> 00:01:15.950
Good to see you again.

00:01:15.950 --> 00:01:17.619
Awesome to see you, my friend.

00:01:17.619 --> 00:01:19.370
This is a really great place, actually.

00:01:19.370 --> 00:01:21.956
Probably one of the more productive areas
is along the river.

00:01:21.956 --> 00:01:23.833
And then I would absolutely stop at 

00:01:23.833 --> 00:01:26.711
Mule Ears Overlook and the Chisos Mountains.

00:01:26.711 --> 00:01:28.254
Appreciate you.

00:01:30.924 --> 00:01:32.967
This is exactly why I love Big Bend,

00:01:32.967 --> 00:01:36.179
because around every corner is a
completely different landscape.

00:01:36.179 --> 00:01:39.599
We've got rivers, we've got mountains,
we've got desert.

00:01:39.599 --> 00:01:44.229
That brings an eclectic character group
when it comes to wildlife.

00:01:44.771 --> 00:01:47.732
But things like black bears,
pumas, bobcats,

00:01:47.732 --> 00:01:50.610
they're really difficult
to see with your own eyeballs.

00:01:50.610 --> 00:01:54.072
So I've set camera traps all up and down
Big Bend National Park.

00:01:54.405 --> 00:01:57.283
Whenever an animal walks by,
the camera takes a photo.

00:01:58.535 --> 00:02:01.329
It's always like Christmas morning
when you check a trap camera.

00:02:03.039 --> 00:02:05.125
Let's go get some mud on these tires.

00:02:08.461 --> 00:02:11.506
The first time I came to Big Bend,
we did it by horseback.

00:02:11.506 --> 00:02:13.883
I've got a lot more horsepower
this time around.

00:02:20.974 --> 00:02:23.560
Pop this long lens on, charge some batteries,

00:02:23.560 --> 00:02:25.812
and then hopefully go and find some wildlife.

00:02:26.563 --> 00:02:30.108
Hold on. Don't come down any further
because we got some animal tracks right here.

00:02:30.108 --> 00:02:31.484
That's definitely coyote.

00:02:31.484 --> 00:02:34.821
You can always tell the difference
between cat and dog paw marks

00:02:34.821 --> 00:02:37.824
because dogs don't retract their claws
when they walk.

00:02:38.366 --> 00:02:40.326
They’re going to come in here
to snag some water,

00:02:40.326 --> 00:02:42.662
and that's why we got the trap
camera right there.

00:02:47.709 --> 00:02:48.793
Set it back up.

00:02:48.793 --> 00:02:50.128
Let me check my frame.

00:02:50.128 --> 00:02:52.297
The only way to
do that is to become the cat.

00:02:55.717 --> 00:02:56.676
Perfect.

00:03:02.182 --> 00:03:04.434
Settling into a circumstance

00:03:04.434 --> 00:03:08.146
where all you do is
have hope that it's going to turn out okay

00:03:08.146 --> 00:03:11.941
and rely on your skill set, your passion,
and your motivation to get you through -

00:03:13.026 --> 00:03:15.278
that is where the magic happens.

00:03:15.278 --> 00:03:16.779
Oh, look at all these swifts right now.

00:03:16.779 --> 00:03:19.657
They're all just over our heads.

00:03:19.657 --> 00:03:21.951
Oh, what a cool bird.

00:03:21.951 --> 00:03:24.287
If I was a swift,
this is where I would live.

00:03:24.287 --> 00:03:27.665
The biggest question
I get is how difficult is my job?

00:03:27.665 --> 00:03:30.376
And maybe for someone else
it might be, you know,

00:03:30.376 --> 00:03:32.503
one of the most challenging things
you can think of.

00:03:32.503 --> 00:03:36.341
But I couldn't think of anything else
I would rather do on the planet.

00:03:36.758 --> 00:03:40.720
It's the easiest job in the world
because it's where my passion drives me to be

00:03:40.720 --> 00:03:45.225
is out there in nature
chasing that next wildlife encounter.

